EXPERIMENT 31 – BLACK-BOX TESTING ON LOGIN PAGE USING SELENIUM
AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to execute black-box testing on a login page.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the selenium-java (Selenium 4) dependency to pom.xml.
2. Selenium Manager downloads the browser driver automatically.
3. Prepare four black-box test cases: valid login, wrong password, blank username and blank password.
4. Store test cases in a two-dimensional array containing username, password and expected result.
5. For every test case:
   - Delete all cookies.
   - Open the login page.
   - Enter username and password.
   - Click the Login button.
6. Compare the actual result (URL or error message) with the expected result and display PASS or FAIL.
7. Close the browser and stop.
CODE
Exercise31.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;

public class Exercise31 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            String[][] cases = {
                {"standard_user", "secret_sauce", "inventory"},
                {"standard_user", "wrong_pass",
                 "Epic sadface: Username and password do not match any user in this service"},
                {"", "secret_sauce",
                 "Epic sadface: Username is required"},
                {"standard_user", "",
                 "Epic sadface: Password is required"}
            };

            int tc = 1;

            for (String[] c : cases) {
                driver.manage().deleteAllCookies();
                driver.get("https://www.saucedemo.com");

                driver.findElement(By.id("user-name")).sendKeys(c[0]);
                driver.findElement(By.id("password")).sendKeys(c[1]);
                driver.findElement(By.id("login-button")).click();

                String actual;

                if (c[2].equals("inventory")) {
                    actual = driver.getCurrentUrl().contains("inventory")
                        ? "inventory" : "login failed";
                } else {
                    actual = driver.findElement(
                        By.cssSelector("[data-test='error']")
                    ).getText();
                }

                System.out.println("TC" + tc + " : " +
                    (actual.equals(c[2]) ? "PASS" : "FAIL"));

                tc++;
            }
        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
Test Case	Username	Password	Expected Result
TC1	standard_user	secret_sauce	Inventory page
TC2	standard_user	wrong_pass	Invalid credentials error
TC3	Blank	secret_sauce	Username is required
TC4	standard_user	Blank	Password is required

OUTPUT
TC1 : PASS
TC2 : PASS
TC3 : PASS
TC4 : PASS


RESULT
